<!--
  Linux-side (AutoSD edge ECU) CycloneDDS config for the X5H RPMsg-backed
  DDS link (Task 8). Frozen wire constants, shared with the CR52 firmware
  side (actuation_module/freertos_x5h/CMakeLists.txt's CONFIG_DDS_* block):
    - domain 2
    - CR52 unicast SPDP peer: 172.16.52.2 (tap0 carries the RPMsg netif;
      see task-9/task-10's `ip tuntap add ... && ip addr add
      172.16.52.1/24 dev tap0`)
    - multicast disabled: the RPMsg link is point-to-point, so there is no
      multicast to fall back on in either direction.

  NOTE (Task 8 self-review): the actuation_module DDS wrapper
  (common/dds/dds.hpp / config.hpp) calls dds_create_domain_with_rawconfig()
  with a programmatic ddsi_config, then dds_create_participant() on the same
  domain id; CycloneDDS reuses the already-created domain and its raw
  config in that case and never parses CYCLONEDDS_URI. This file is not
  consulted at runtime by dds_pub/dds_sub built from
  freertos_s32z2/edge_ecu_peer/CMakeLists.txt; it exists as the documented,
  checkable record of the Linux-side wire constants (validated by
  check-dds-config.sh) and for any future CycloneDDS consumer on this host
  that does honor CYCLONEDDS_URI. The peer binaries get these same values
  baked in at build time via -DCONFIG_DDS_DOMAIN_ID / -DCONFIG_DDS_NETWORK_INTERFACE
  / -DCONFIG_DDS_PEER and a CONFIG_DDS_DISABLE_MULTICAST compile definition
  (see scripts/build-edge-ecu-peer-arm64.sh).
-->
<CycloneDDS>
  <Domain Id="2">
    <General>
      <Interfaces><NetworkInterface name="tap0"/></Interfaces>
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <Peers><Peer Address="172.16.52.2"/></Peers>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
